Relevant tables & columns for the task  

• `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`  
  – `id`: unique key, needed for possible joins or extra checks.  
  – `title`: the full question title; we will look for titles that start with / contain “how”.  
  – `tags`: angle‑bracket delimited tag list; we will look for any of the Android‑related tags (`android-layout`, `android-activity`, `android-intent`, …).  
  – `view_count`: the per‑question view counter that lets us decide which question is “most viewed”.  

Useful filter conditions  

1. Tag match (case insensitive, angle‑bracket formatted)  
   ```
   WHERE LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
          OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-activity>%'
          OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-intent>%'
          …                           -- add more tags as needed
   ```  

2. Title beginning / containing “how” (case‑insensitive)  
   ```
   AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'       -- starts with “how ”
   --   or
   AND LOWER(title) LIKE '% how %'     -- contains the word “how”
   ```  

3. Get the single most‑viewed row  
   ```
   ORDER BY view_count DESC
   LIMIT 1
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → final SQL queries
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1) Peek at some Android‑layout questions
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Same, but only questions whose title starts with “How”
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Check distinct Android‑specific tags that appear together with “how” questions
SELECT DISTINCT tag
FROM (
  SELECT SPLIT(REGEXP_REPLACE(tags, '[<>]', ''), '|') AS taglist
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
  WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
        AND tags LIKE '%android%'
), UNNEST(taglist) AS tag
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Combine several Android tags and fetch a small sample
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE (
  LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-activity>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-intent>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-fragment>%'
)
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE '% how %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Which Android “how” questions have the biggest score?
SELECT id, title, score, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE (LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-%')
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
ORDER BY score DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Narrow to the three tags we care about; sort by view_count
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE (
  LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-activity>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-intent>%'
)
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same as (6) but remove community wiki questions (if any)
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE community_owned_date IS NULL
  AND (
    LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
    OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-activity>%'
    OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-intent>%'
  )
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Add all common Android tags and show the top 20 by views
WITH android_tags AS (
  SELECT '%<android-layout>%'  AS t UNION ALL
  SELECT '%<android-activity>%' UNION ALL
  SELECT '%<android-intent>%'  UNION ALL
  SELECT '%<android-fragment>%' UNION ALL
  SELECT '%<android-viewpager>%'
)
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM android_tags
    WHERE LOWER(tags) LIKE LOWER(t)
)
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Show the current candidate for “most viewed” (single record)
SELECT title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE (
  LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-activity>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-intent>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-fragment>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-viewpager>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-studio>%'
)
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: retrieve the title of the single most‑viewed
-- “how” Android‑development question across the targeted tags
SELECT title AS most_viewed_android_how_question
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE (
  LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-layout>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-activity>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-intent>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-fragment>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-viewpager>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android-animation>%'
  OR LOWER(tags) LIKE '%<android>%'
)
  AND LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 1;
```
